#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305622 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b6bb984-cc93-594c-a50a-8758d6705134" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\pi ,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305624} {:answer/id #uuid "7363486d-b4cc-5260-9758-a74e6f12f2e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305625} {:answer/id #uuid "9eaf2a1d-32c6-53c2-a02e-71ffd3d34809" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305626} {:answer/id #uuid "a6ef94a1-7bb3-5151-9fa4-219556ec4305" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,4\\pi ,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305627} {:answer/id #uuid "d287f358-b8b4-5b30-b0cf-4ec44342fb4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,1,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305628}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7363486d-b4cc-5260-9758-a74e6f12f2e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305625} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdd9714f-d529-5a8e-9a9e-6f07a2c5dc7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305623}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0cef1288-682b-5449-bd6c-f4cbfcbde18f" :question/math-academy-id "q-128452" :question/problem "Find the value of $(2f(t)-g(t))^{′}$ at $t=-1,$ if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨8\\sqrt{3-t},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t),\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t)⟩, \\\\ g(t) & =⟨{t}^{2}-t,\\,\\pi {t}^{2},\\,1-{t}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that\n\n$$\n(2f(t)-g(t))^{′}=2{f}^{′}(t)-{g}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8\\sqrt{3-t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{3-t}},\\,\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t),\\,\\frac{1}{t}⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\pi {t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t-1,\\,2\\pi t,\\,-2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2f(-1)-g(-1))^{′} & =2{f}^{′}(-1)-{g}^{′}(-1) \\\\  & =2⟨-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{3-(-1)}},\\,\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\pi ),\\,\\frac{1}{(-1)}⟩-⟨2(-1)-1,\\,2\\pi (-1),\\,-2(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =2⟨-2,-\\pi ,-1⟩-⟨-3,-2\\pi ,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,-2\\pi ,-2⟩-⟨-3,-2\\pi ,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
